From: TB371FC research contributors <tb371fc-research@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] input: nt36523: propagate restart errors and release resources

Probe and resume used to report success after failed firmware download;
resume also discarded the reset-state and pen-command results. Keep the
IRQ disabled until initialization completes, propagate failures, and
leave a failed resume quiescent and retryable. Check deep-sleep and IRQ
wake operations, track wake ownership and disarm it on resume/removal.
An aborted suspend restores the active software state and reports error.

Do not run an IRQ thread on partially initialized probe state. Reject IRQ
zero as well as preserving negative mapping errors. Handle MT allocation
failure. Balance the probe wake hold, drain event work before ESD/IRQ
teardown, and free SPI and per-download firmware buffers. No new gesture,
panel sequencing, CTN730, or electrical timing protocol is introduced.

Applies after 0018-input-nt36523-use-declared-physical-dimensions.patch.

diff --git a/drivers/input/touchscreen/nt36523/nt36xxx.c b/drivers/input/touchscreen/nt36523/nt36xxx.c
--- a/drivers/input/touchscreen/nt36523/nt36xxx.c
+++ b/drivers/input/touchscreen/nt36523/nt36xxx.c
@@ -80,6 +80,20 @@
 			ts->irq_enabled = false;
 		}
 	}
+}
+
+static int nvt_irq_set_wake(bool enable)
+{
+	int ret;
+
+	if (ts->irq_wake_enabled == enable)
+		return 0;
+	ret = enable ? enable_irq_wake(ts->client->irq) :
+		       disable_irq_wake(ts->client->irq);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+	ts->irq_wake_enabled = enable;
+	return 0;
 }
 
 static inline int32_t spi_read_write(struct spi_device *client, uint8_t *buf, size_t len , NVT_SPI_RW rw)
@@ -1353,13 +1367,19 @@
 static void nvt_suspend_work(struct work_struct *work)
 {
 	struct nvt_ts_data *ts_core = container_of(work, struct nvt_ts_data, suspend_work);
-	nvt_ts_suspend(&ts_core->client->dev);
+	int ret = nvt_ts_suspend(&ts_core->client->dev);
+
+	if (ret)
+		NVT_ERR("asynchronous suspend failed: %d\n", ret);
 }
 
 static void nvt_resume_work(struct work_struct *work)
 {
 	struct nvt_ts_data *ts_core = container_of(work, struct nvt_ts_data, resume_work);
-	nvt_ts_resume(&ts_core->client->dev);
+	int ret = nvt_ts_resume(&ts_core->client->dev);
+
+	if (ret)
+		NVT_ERR("asynchronous resume failed: %d\n", ret);
 }
 
